/T (Risk heatmap is a simple visual tool that plots risks based on impact  and likelihood. Each risk is positioned as a point in the matrix. A defined acceptance threshold \(line of acceptance\) separates tolerable risks from critical ones. Risks above the line require mitigation, while risks below can typically be accepted or monitored. Movement of risks over time shows how likelihood or impact may change.)
/E (Risk heatmap is a simple visual tool that plots risks based on impact  and likelihood. Each risk is positioned as a point in the matrix. A defined acceptance threshold \(line of acceptance\) separates tolerable risks from critical ones. Risks above the line require mitigation, while risks below can typically be accepted or monitored. Movement of risks over time shows how likelihood or impact may change.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [20]
>>
