747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (Procurement without crises is neither realistic nor necessarily desirable. In some cases, it can be economically sensible to accept identified risks. In particular, risks with low probability but extremely high impact present a challenge as preventive measures are often difficult to justify in advance. At the same time, unexpected risks will always occur.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
748 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
/E (As a result, crises are an inherent part of procurement. This is why 15M Risk Management places strong emphasis on strengthening procurement capabilities to manage disruptions effectively. The 15M Maturity Analysis for crisis resilience builds on this by systematically identifying and addressing improvement potential.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
749 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 138 0 R
