823 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Materials with elevated risk exposure require careful management in procurement. Given the large number of materials, risk assessment should be kept simple and, where possible, automated. Both cause-oriented and impact-oriented approaches can be applied:)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [68]
>>
endobj
824 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2613 0 R
/E (Cause-oriented approach: Materials are assessed based on characteristics that indicate vulnerability, such as supplier structure or complexity. For example, materials with a single or sole supplier, or those requiring licenses or specialized tooling, are considered higher risk. These dimensions can be combined into a structured risk classification.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [69]
>>
endobj
825 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2614 0 R
/E (Impact-oriented approach: The potential financial impact of a material disruption, such as loss of revenue, is assessed using impact-based analysis. This provides a benchmark for evaluating the criticality of materials.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [70]
>>
endobj
826 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2615 0 R
/E (Combined view: Integrating both approaches results in a consolidated material risk classification, enabling prioritization \(e.g., from low to very high risk\).)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [71]
>>
endobj
827 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2616 0 R
/E (Risk clusters: Materials with shared risk drivers are grouped into risk clusters, for example, by all materials. These clusters require focused and proactive management.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [72]
>>
endobj
828 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Materials or risk clusters with high risk exposure require careful management in procurement. Risk analysis should remain simple and can be conducted using both cause-oriented criteria and impact-oriented measures.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [73]
>>
