<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (15M Maturity Management assesses the maturity of the Procurement Management System \(PMS\) and identifies areas for improvement. Particular emphasis can be placed on risk-related aspects, especially the level of implementation of the seven building blocks. The identified improvement opportunities are translated into strategic options and integrated into the Procurement Framework Strategy, where they are prioritized alongside other initiatives, consolidated into a coherent strategy, and implemented.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1053 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (In practice, this drives a continuous strategic transformation. For example, in one case, maturity assessments were conducted regularly over several years, complemented by iterative updates of the Framework Strategy. Development typically follows a step-by-step approach: starting with the management of top risks, followed by the introduction of category and supplier risk management, and later expanding to resilience-oriented approaches.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1054 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Overall, risk management capabilities are progressively developed and professionalized over time. )
