1280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 148 0 R
/T (Ideal approach:)
/E (Ideal approach:)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1281 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 148 0 R
/T (The implementation of 15M Risk Management is embedded within the broader strategic transformation of procurement using the 15M Architecture. This approach starts with a risk-oriented maturity assessment within the Procurement Framework Strategy. The assessment can be conducted at varying levels of depth, from a basic inventory based on the 15 modules to a more advanced evaluation with a maturity score. In both cases, the objective is to identify and prioritize improvement opportunities. Based on these insights, the Framework Strategy defines strategic directions to establish or further develop key elements of the Procurement Management System.)
/E (The implementation of 15M Risk Management is embedded within the broader strategic transformation of procurement using the 15M Architecture. This approach starts with a risk-oriented maturity assessment within the Procurement Framework Strategy. The assessment can be conducted at varying levels of depth, from a basic inventory based on the 15 modules to a more advanced evaluation with a maturity score. In both cases, the objective is to identify and prioritize improvement opportunities. Based on these insights, the Framework Strategy defines strategic directions to establish or further develop key elements of the Procurement Management System.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 148 0 R
/T (Approach without 15M Architecture:)
/E (Approach without 15M Architecture:)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 148 0 R
/T (Even without adopting the full 15M Architecture, procurement risk management can be implemented using the 15M Risk Management building blocks. In this case, the current implementation level of each building block is assessed and areas for improvement are identified and prioritized. The building blocks can then be implemented step by step in a pragmatic manner. )
/E (Even without adopting the full 15M Architecture, procurement risk management can be implemented using the 15M Risk Management building blocks. In this case, the current implementation level of each building block is assessed and areas for improvement are identified and prioritized. The building blocks can then be implemented step by step in a pragmatic manner. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 148 0 R
/T (In parallel, the Risk Management System \(Building Block7\) should be gradually developed to ensure consistent integration across procurement activities.)
/E (In parallel, the Risk Management System \(Building Block7\) should be gradually developed to ensure consistent integration across procurement activities.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 148 0 R
/T (Overall, the guiding principle is simple: start wherever you are and professionalize step by step.)
